course: dictionary
lesson: 13376
title: A safe place to rest
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A haven is a safe, peaceful place where people or animals can rest or be protected. When you meet haven in a story, look at the words around it: they are its context, and they leave clues. «The storm was rough, but the little cottage was a haven.» Rough storms are scary, so a haven must be a place where you feel safe.
explain: Haven is a noun, so you can say a haven or havens. Try it in a sentence: «The nature reserve is a haven for wildlife.» Does your meaning fit? A nature reserve is a safe place for animals, so the meaning works.
explain: Long ago, a haven meant a harbour where ships could shelter from bad weather. That is an old use, and you may see it in old books or in place names such as Newhaven. Today, most people use haven to mean a safe, peaceful place.
fact: A haven is a safe, peaceful place where people or animals can rest or be protected.
fact: «Haven» can also mean an old word for a harbour, where ships shelter.
fact: A tax haven is a country where people put money to pay less tax.
fact: A nature reserve can be a haven for wildlife, because animals are protected there.
fact: Some place names, such as Newhaven, come from the old meaning of harbour.
exercise: «The tired puppy curled up in its haven by the warm fire.» What is a haven here? | A cold, wet hole in the garden | A loud room full of people | *A safe, peaceful place to rest
exercise: «The old ships sailed into the haven before the storm.» Haven here is an old word. What does it mean? | *A harbour where ships can shelter | A ship with a broken sail | A deep, dark sea | A shop that sells fish
exercise: «Some companies move their money to a tax haven to pay less tax.» What is a tax haven? | A type of boat | *A country where people put money to pay less tax | A school for maths | A place where you can swim all year
test: «The library was a haven of quiet on a noisy day.» What does haven of quiet suggest? | *A peaceful, quiet place | A dark cave | A busy shop | A place full of shouting
test: Why might the place name Newhaven be linked to ships? | Because it has a big park | *Because haven once meant a harbour | Because it is very cold | Because it has a new school
exam: «Mum said home should be a safe haven for us.» What does safe haven suggest? | A loud, busy car | A place with lots of rules | A shop that sells toys | *A place where you feel protected and calm
